{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"MGASA-2026-0101","published":"2026-04-18T02:40:55Z","modified":"2026-04-18T02:45:29.673659Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-41035"],"summary":"Updated rsync packages fix security vulnerability","details":"In rsync 3.0.1 through 3.4.1, receive_xattr relies on an untrusted\nlength value during a qsort call, leading to a receiver use-after-free.\nThe victim must run rsync with -X (aka --xattrs). On Linux, many (but\nnot all) common configurations are vulnerable. Non-Linux platforms are\nmore widely vulnerable. (CVE-2026-41035)\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsync","ecosystem":"Mageia:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/mageia/rsync?arch=source&distro=mageia-9"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.2.7-1.4.mga9"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"section":"core"},"database_specific":{"source":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0101.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://advisories.mageia.org/MGASA-2026-0101.html"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugs.mageia.org/show_bug.cgi?id=35373"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/16/2"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/04/16/9"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://github.com/RsyncProject/rsync/issues/871"}],"credits":[{"name":"Mageia","contact":["https://wiki.mageia.org/en/Packages_Security_Team"],"type":"COORDINATOR"}]}